/**
@page api_qsys Queueing Systems
@brief Single-station queueing system analysis

The qsys module provides exact and approximate formulas for single-station queueing systems,
including M/M/1, M/M/k, M/G/1, G/I/G/1 approximations, and finite buffer loss models.

@subsection alg_qsys_list Function List

<b>Basic Queueing Models:</b>

- @ref qsys_mm1 "qsys_mm1" - M/M/1 queue: mean waiting time
- @ref qsys_mmk "qsys_mmk" - M/M/k queue: mean waiting time with Erlang-C formula
- @ref qsys_mg1 "qsys_mg1" - M/G/1 queue: Pollaczek-Khinchine formula
- @ref qsys_gm1 "qsys_gm1" - G/M/1 queue: mean waiting time

<b>G/I/G/1 Approximations:</b>

- @ref qsys_gig1_ubnd_kingman "qsys_gig1_ubnd_kingman" - Kingman's upper bound for G/I/G/1
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_allencunneen "qsys_gig1_approx_allencunneen" - Allen-Cunneen approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_gelenbe "qsys_gig1_approx_gelenbe" - Gelenbe approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_heyman "qsys_gig1_approx_heyman" - Heyman approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_kimura "qsys_gig1_approx_kimura" - Kimura approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_klb "qsys_gig1_approx_klb" - Kramer-Langenbach-Belz approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_kobayashi "qsys_gig1_approx_kobayashi" - Kobayashi approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_marchal "qsys_gig1_approx_marchal" - Marchal approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_myskja "qsys_gig1_approx_myskja" - Myskja approximation
- @ref qsys_gig1_approx_myskja2 "qsys_gig1_approx_myskja2" - Myskja improved approximation

<b>G/I/G/k Approximations:</b>

- @ref qsys_gigk_approx "qsys_gigk_approx" - G/I/G/k multiserver approximation
- @ref qsys_gigk_approx_kingman "qsys_gigk_approx_kingman" - Kingman approximation for G/I/G/k

<b>Finite Buffer Loss Models:</b>

- @ref qsys_mm1k_loss "qsys_mm1k_loss" - M/M/1/K loss probability
- @ref qsys_mg1k_loss "qsys_mg1k_loss" - M/G/1/K loss probability (Niu-Cooper)
- @ref qsys_mg1k_loss_mgs "qsys_mg1k_loss_mgs" - M/G/1/K loss probability (MacGregor Smith)

@anchor qsys_mm1
### qsys_mm1
  <b>Description:</b> M/M/1 queue mean waiting time.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [W, rho] = qsys_mm1(lambda, mu)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Service rate</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Mean waiting time (including service)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rho</td><td>Utilization</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor qsys_mmk
### qsys_mmk
  <b>Description:</b> M/M/k queue mean waiting time using Erlang-C formula.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [W, rho] = qsys_mmk(lambda, mu, k)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Service rate per server</td></tr>
  <tr><td>k</td><td>Number of servers</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Mean waiting time (including service)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rho</td><td>Utilization per server</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor qsys_mg1
### qsys_mg1
  <b>Description:</b> M/G/1 queue using the Pollaczek-Khinchine formula.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [W, rhohat] = qsys_mg1(lambda, mu, cs)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Service rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>cs</td><td>Coefficient of variation of service time</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Mean waiting time (including service)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rhohat</td><td>Effective utilization for M/M/1 equivalence</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor qsys_gm1
### qsys_gm1
  <b>Description:</b> G/M/1 queue mean waiting time.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  W = qsys_gm1(sigma, mu)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>sigma</td><td>Load at arrival instants (Laplace transform of inter-arrival times)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Service rate</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Mean waiting time (including service)</td></tr>
  </table>

@anchor qsys_gig1_ubnd_kingman
### qsys_gig1_ubnd_kingman
  <b>Description:</b> Kingman's upper bound for G/I/G/1 queue.

  <b>Syntax:</b>
  @code
  [W, rhohat] = qsys_gig1_ubnd_kingman(lambda, mu, ca, cs)
  @endcode

  <b>Parameters:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>lambda</td><td>Arrival rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>mu</td><td>Service rate</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ca</td><td>Coefficient of variation of inter-arrival times</td></tr>
  <tr><td>cs</td><td>Coefficient of variation of service times</td></tr>
  </table>

  <b>Returns:</b>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>W</td><td>Upper bound on mean waiting time</td></tr>
  <tr><td>rhohat</td><td>Effective utilization</td></tr>
  </table>

